abstract: >-
  Maple worksheets and procedures, with MATLAB scripts, for the scalar, vector and tensor quasinormal modes of
  Schwarzschild–Tangherlini black holes corrected by a Gauss–Bonnet term, in dimensions 5 to 26. A Chebyshev
  collocation of the compactified radial equation in multiprecision arithmetic gives a quadratic eigenvalue problem
  solved with polyeig and the Advanpix toolbox, and five scripts fit straight lines to the spacing of the purely
  imaginary modes against the multipole.
